WEBVTT Original fictional workflow interview

NOTE Fictional speakers and scripted captions. No recording was verified.

intro
00:00.000 --> 00:07.250
<v Morgan>How do you keep a small project handoff understandable?</v>

source
00:07.250 --> 00:17.500
<v Rowan>Start with the original source. Keep it beside the edited version so another person can compare them.</v>

ownership
00:17.500 --> 00:28.125
<v Morgan>We also name the next action and the person responsible for it. That is more useful than a vague status label.</v>

review
00:28.125 --> 00:39.875
<v Rowan>When words are uncertain, mark them for review. A readable draft should not hide uncertainty in the source.</v>

export
00:39.875 --> 00:51.000 align:start
<v Morgan>Package the transcript, timestamps, and originals together. The next editor should not need to reconstruct the context.</v>

finish
00:51.000 --> 01:02.500
<v Rowan>A useful handoff makes the next action easy without pretending the work is already finished.</v>
